nodecode-reaction-feedback is a rewrite of AhmetArif0's AhmetArif0/hermes-reaction-feedback:
https://github.com/AhmetArif0/hermes-reaction-feedback
commit 50d8dbd0fb9f89ce1002ad378a8b656e52a617e1
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 AhmetArif0 (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's three gateway hooks became one cell. Its Telegram
message and reaction hooks are the `ask` and `record` actions of the `reaction_feedback`
tool, which a chat surface (or the model) calls; its in-memory ledger is kept per
conversation with the same attribution rule — a reaction belongs to the turn whose user
message it sits under — and its `pre_llm_call` injection became a harness section read at
the start of the turn, so the note arrives by itself and is taken once. The wording of
the note is the original's, and so are the bounds: how much of a message is quoted, how
many messages, reactions and conversations are kept, and how long a reaction waits.
What was left out: the Telegram-only reading of gateway payloads. Nodecode's chat rooms
report what they see, so the cell takes `chat` and `message_id` as ordinary strings and
integers rather than parsing a platform's update objects, and the per-profile home is
gone because a Nodecode home is already one process with one ledger.
